card.statement:
Let $(M;\rho,\gamma)$ be a weak module over $(A,m,\eta,L, \mu, \alpha, \beta)$. Then the triple $(M;\rho,\gamma_A)$ forms a weak module over $(A,m,\eta,L\otimes A, \mu_A, \alpha_{A}, \beta_A)$, where

\begin{equation*}
\gamma_A \ =
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0.5, 0.5) -- (0.25, 0.75)--(0.25,1);
\draw[bmod] (0.5, 0) -- (0, 0.5)--(0.25,0.75);
\draw[bmod] (0.75, 0) -- (0.75, 0.25)--(0.25,0.75);
\btoken{0.25, 0.75}{east}{\rho};
\btoken{0.5, 0.5}{west}{\gamma};
\end{tikzpicture} \ .
\end{equation*}
